{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"stripe sandbox create --help 2>&1 | sed -n '1,220p'\"","aggregated_output":"Create a new Stripe sandbox with test API keys.\n\nIf you are already logged in (have a configured API key), opens the\nsandbox management page in your browser instead.\n\nOtherwise, uses a proof-of-work challenge to provision a temporary sandbox\nwithout authentication. If that fails, automatically falls back to\nbrowser-based signup/login.\n\nKeys are saved to the current CLI profile so subsequent stripe commands\nwork immediately.\n\nUsage:\n  stripe sandbox create [flags]\n\nExamples:\n  stripe sandbox create --email you@example.com\n  stripe sandbox create --from-git\n\n[Agent guidance]\n  Provisions a sandbox and saves keys to the current CLI profile.\n  Pass --from-git to resolve your email from git config user.email.\n  Pass --email to provide an explicit email address.\n  Falls back to browser login on server errors.\n  If you do not have an account: run stripe sandbox create (provisions a claimable sandbox without a browser).\n  If you already have a key: use --api-key (or set STRIPE_API_KEY).\n  Run stripe --map to quickly see all available commands.\n  Run stripe resources to discover all available API resources.\n  Run stripe [resource] --help to see operations and required/common parameters for a resource.\n  Run stripe help [resource] [operation] to see the full parameter list for a specific operation.\n\n\nFlags:\n      --email string       Your email address\n      --from-git           Infer email and full name from git config\n      --full-name string   Your full name (optional)\n  -h, --help               help for create\n      --non-interactive    Print output directly without waiting for input\n\nGlobal flags:\n      --api-key string        Your API key to use for the command\n      --color string          turn on/off color output (on, off, auto)\n      --config string         config file (default is\n                              $HOME/.config/stripe/config.toml)\n      --device-name string    device name\n      --log-level string      log level (debug, info, trace, warn, error)\n                              (default \"info\")\n      --map string[=\"tree\"]   Print a command tree [tree|compact|paths|json]\n  -p, --project-name string   the project name to read from for config\n                              (default \"default\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find current official Prodigi Print API sandbox documentation for creating a print-on-demand apparel order, especially Classic/standard black t-shirts, product SKU conventions for fitted/women's and unisex sizes S/M/L/XL, order JSON schema, print area/artwork asset URL requirements, sandbox base URL, dry-run or test behavior, and quote endpoint. Return official documentation URLs and exact example request bodies where available."},"result":null,"error":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"toolshed_web_search","tool":"call_web_search","arguments":{"fast_mode":false,"web_search_instructions":"Find current official Prodigi Print API sandbox documentation for creating a print-on-demand apparel order, especially Classic/standard black t-shirts, product SKU conventions for fitted/women's and unisex sizes S/M/L/XL, order JSON schema, print area/artwork asset URL requirements, sandbox base URL, dry-run or test behavior, and quote endpoint. Return official documentation URLs and exact example request bodies where available."},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Research Report: Prodigi Print API Sandbox Documentation for Creating Print-on-Demand Apparel Orders\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nProdigi's Print API provides a comprehensive solution for creating print-on-demand apparel orders, including classic black t-shirts. The API offers detailed documentation on product SKUs, order JSON schemas, print area specifications, artwork asset URL requirements, sandbox environment usage, test behaviors, and quote endpoints. This report consolidates key information from official Prodigi sources to facilitate seamless integration and order processing.\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **Finding 1:** Prodigi offers both sandbox and live environments for API integration, with the sandbox environment (`https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`) designed for testing without incurring charges or fulfilling orders. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 2:** Product SKUs for apparel items, such as classic black t-shirts, can be retrieved using the Product Details endpoint (`/v4.0/products/{sku}`), which provides comprehensive information including valid attributes and print area specifications. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 3:** The order JSON schema requires specifying the product SKU, recipient details, shipping method, and assets (artwork URLs). Assets must be provided as publicly accessible URLs in JPG or PNG format. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/?utm_source=openai))\n\n- **Finding 4:** The Quote endpoint allows users to obtain pricing information for orders without creating them, facilitating cost estimation during the development phase. ([prodigi.com](https://www.prodigi.com/faq/print-api/?utm_source=openai))\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Source Analysis\n\n### Source 1: Prodigi API Documentation\n\n- **URL:** https://www.prodigi.com/print-api/docs/reference/\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** Official Documentation\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official API documentation)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe Prodigi API documentation provides a comprehensive reference for integrating print-on-demand services. It details the RESTful API structure, authentication methods, and order processing workflows. The documentation emphasizes the availability of both sandbox and live environments, with the sandbox environment (`https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`) intended for testing purposes without incurring charges or fulfilling orders. Authentication is managed via an `X-API-Key` header, and the API accepts `application/json` payloads, returning JSON responses.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `https://api.prodigi.com`\n\n- Authentication Header: `X-API-Key`\n\n- Payload Format: `application/json`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"Sandbox is our testing environment. It will not fulfil your orders, and you will not be charged for using it.\"\n\n> \"Each request to our API requires the use of an authentication header: `X-API-Key`.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 2: How to Place your First Order with the Prodigi Print API\n\n- **URL:** https://www.prodigi.com/blog/your-first-print-api-order/\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** March 19, 2021\n\n- **Source Type:** Blog Post\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official blog post)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThis guide walks through the process of placing an order using the Prodigi Print API. It emphasizes the importance of selecting the correct product SKU, which can be obtained via the Product Details endpoint (`/v4.0/products/{sku}`). The guide provides an example of creating an order by sending a POST request to `/v4.0/orders/` with a JSON payload that includes the product SKU, recipient details, shipping method, and assets (artwork URLs). Assets must be provided as publicly accessible URLs in JPG or PNG format.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Product Details Endpoint: `/v4.0/products/{sku}`\n\n- Order Creation Endpoint: `/v4.0/orders/`\n\n- Accepted Asset Formats: JPG, PNG\n\n- Example SKU: `GLOBAL-FAP-16x24`\n\n**Notable Quotes:**\n\n> \"You can find a product on our site, by browsing the dashboard, by downloading our product catalogue, or... by using our lookup endpoints.\"\n\n> \"We accept jpg and png format images. For some products we may recommend one format over the other.\"\n\n---\n\n### Source 3: Print API | FAQ | Prodigi\n\n- **URL:** https://www.prodigi.com/faq/print-api/\n\n- **Domain:** prodigi.com\n\n- **Publication Date:** Date not specified\n\n- **Source Type:** FAQ\n\n- **Credibility:** High (Official FAQ)\n\n**Summary:**\n\nThe FAQ section addresses common queries related to the Prodigi Print API. It clarifies the differences between the sandbox and live environments, noting that the sandbox environment does not charge or fulfill orders, making it suitable for testing. The FAQ also explains the use of the Quote endpoint, which allows users to obtain pricing information for orders without creating them. Additionally, it provides guidance on image file types accepted by the API (JPG, PNG, PDF) and how to handle image sizing and cropping.\n\n**Key Data Points:**\n\n- Sandbox API URL: `https://api.sandbox.prodigi.com`\n\n- Live API URL: `https://api.prodigi.com`\n\n- � "}],"_meta":{"openai/widgetSessionId":"7b81a5f1-61b0-413e-9e72-077e5137587a"},"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
